          "path": "_m/9/x/m/1/ames-monument-wp/american-pyramid.jpg",
          "filename": "American Pyramid.jpg",
          "caption": "In the dark a monument lies,\nA relic of an era unseen.\n‘Neath stars aplenty in Wyoming skies\nIt remembers an engine’s full steam.\nThe granite sides and sloping walls\nRise from the prairie at night.\nThe stars above, a hallowed hall,\nMake an incredible sight.\nThe American Pyramid.\nThe Ames Monument, near Laramie, WY, marks the highest point on the original transcontinental railroad and was built between 1880 and 1882. Now, nearly 150 years later, the rails and old town have vanished into time, relics of a bygone era. \n\nThis photograph was taken on the evening of July 2, 2024, using a Canon EOS RP and RF 16mm STM lens.",
